WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.120 --> 00:00:03.120
You're an entrepreneur.

00:00:03.120 --> 00:00:06.930
You just started a business and you're asking
that question everybody struggles with.

00:00:06.930 --> 00:00:10.559
Who do I hire first as my first employee?

00:00:10.559 --> 00:00:16.430
Do I hire somebody in sales, marketing, operations,
accounting, finance, product development,

00:00:16.430 --> 00:00:17.430
legal.

00:00:17.430 --> 00:00:18.759
Who do I hire first?

00:00:18.759 --> 00:00:22.070
Now, before I answer that question for you,
it's a very simple answer.

00:00:22.070 --> 00:00:25.700
But before I answer that question for you,
you got to keep one thing in mind.

00:00:25.700 --> 00:00:30.340
If you're a startup, and you're an entrepreneur,
and you're already funded, you have money,

00:00:30.340 --> 00:00:33.631
that group that gave you the money, is already
expecting you to have a team together, because

00:00:33.631 --> 00:00:37.309
they're not going to give you the money without
you having a team to show here's who I have,

00:00:37.309 --> 00:00:38.309
okay?

00:00:38.309 --> 00:00:41.300
I'm assuming that I'm talking to the group
that doesn't have money today.

00:00:41.300 --> 00:00:42.710
You're without money.

00:00:42.710 --> 00:00:44.980
You're trying to stretch every dollar.

00:00:44.980 --> 00:00:46.940
You're wearing multiple hats yourself.

00:00:46.940 --> 00:00:52.249
Like, you're the CEO, CFO, COO, CMO, you're
every single thing in the company, you're

00:00:52.249 --> 00:00:53.249
doing right now.

00:00:53.249 --> 00:00:54.659
It just so happens your business card says
CEO.

00:00:54.659 --> 00:00:56.850
So who do you hire first?

00:00:56.850 --> 00:01:00.100
Look, you got a lot of departments.

00:01:00.100 --> 00:01:03.199
And a lot of people will tell you who to hire
first.

00:01:03.199 --> 00:01:07.500
For me, it's a very simple thing to be processing
and thinking about.

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:09.070
So look at it this way.

00:01:09.070 --> 00:01:13.730
Any sports team that already has a position,
if a team already has a quarterback, you're

00:01:13.730 --> 00:01:15.300
going to go get another quarterback?

00:01:15.300 --> 00:01:16.300
No.

00:01:16.300 --> 00:01:20.800
If a team already has a very, very strong
center, you going to get another center?

00:01:20.800 --> 00:01:21.800
No.

00:01:21.800 --> 00:01:27.020
If you're running a business, whatever your
strength is, the first person you hire is

00:01:27.020 --> 00:01:28.820
your opposing strength.

00:01:28.820 --> 00:01:30.190
That's your first hire.

00:01:30.190 --> 00:01:31.360
Your opposing strength.

00:01:31.360 --> 00:01:34.070
Well, Pat, what do you mean opposing strength?

00:01:34.070 --> 00:01:40.090
If you're in sales, most salespeople who are
very, very good in sales, are not necessarily

00:01:40.090 --> 00:01:42.540
very good in operations.

00:01:42.540 --> 00:01:46.630
Now if you're very good at operations, you're
probably not very good in sales.

00:01:46.630 --> 00:01:50.640
If you're incredible at product development,
most product development people don't like

00:01:50.640 --> 00:01:53.540
to be around a lot of people , so you need
sales.

00:01:53.540 --> 00:01:58.480
If you're in sales, and you're a great salesperson
like Ray Kroc, but you don't know what product

00:01:58.480 --> 00:02:00.640
to develop, you need somebody here [product
development].

00:02:00.640 --> 00:02:04.640
If you're someone who's very good with money,
and maybe even you have money, but you don't

00:02:04.640 --> 00:02:06.960
have an idea, maybe you meet up there [with
product development].

00:02:06.960 --> 00:02:11.299
But the point I'm making to you here is whatever
your opposing strength is, that's what you

00:02:11.299 --> 00:02:12.670
need to start off with.

00:02:12.670 --> 00:02:15.329
Now, let's say this other thing for you to
be thinking about.

00:02:15.329 --> 00:02:18.049
I'll go dig a little bit deeper.

00:02:18.049 --> 00:02:24.069
In the game of sports, everybody that builds
a team, they generally build it around their

00:02:24.069 --> 00:02:27.960
philosophy of what's the most important thing
to invest their money into.

00:02:27.960 --> 00:02:30.440
Let me explain what I mean by this.

00:02:30.440 --> 00:02:33.010
Some teams build around one player.

00:02:33.010 --> 00:02:37.780
Okay, so for instance, Chicago Bulls, Michael
Jordan, they built around one player.

00:02:37.780 --> 00:02:39.629
Michael Jordan was the main player.

00:02:39.629 --> 00:02:42.870
Then they brought supporting cast to be around
him.

00:02:42.870 --> 00:02:46.800
The San Antonio Spurs builds around a system.

00:02:46.800 --> 00:02:50.060
They're not building around one personality,
one player.

00:02:50.060 --> 00:02:53.030
That's why they've been playing for 20 years,
and they're winning 20 years.

00:02:53.030 --> 00:02:58.689
Whether they go from David Robinson to Duncan
to Lamar, Marcus, Aldridge, and Leonard, it's

00:02:58.689 --> 00:03:02.079
a system they're building it on.

00:03:02.079 --> 00:03:03.079
Right?

00:03:03.079 --> 00:03:06.019
I don't know what you're going to be building
your business and your philosophy and system

00:03:06.019 --> 00:03:07.019
on.

00:03:07.019 --> 00:03:12.299
But what I could tell you is whoever you choose
as your first next, determines what you value

00:03:12.299 --> 00:03:13.859
the most.

00:03:13.859 --> 00:03:19.680
Sometimes, sometimes generally the most logical
people, the people that are most.

00:03:19.680 --> 00:03:25.409
. . and everything is very logical and organized,
like the administrative folks, sometimes they

00:03:25.409 --> 00:03:27.919
think they need this [finance and accounting].

00:03:27.919 --> 00:03:31.079
Sometimes they think they need product development
only.

00:03:31.079 --> 00:03:32.090
Logical.

00:03:32.090 --> 00:03:36.629
Sometimes they just go, everything is just
way too logical, and they forget that you

00:03:36.629 --> 00:03:38.189
need sales.

00:03:38.189 --> 00:03:41.310
If you don't have somebody selling, you don't
have volume revenues coming in.

00:03:41.310 --> 00:03:43.510
If there's no sales going on, done.

00:03:43.510 --> 00:03:45.060
It's just purely a done deal.

00:03:45.060 --> 00:03:46.060
Right?

00:03:46.060 --> 00:03:50.629
So back in the day when a lot of companies
would do very, very well and they would develop

00:03:50.629 --> 00:03:54.609
these guys that would become the CEOs of the
company, everybody who got started with the

00:03:54.609 --> 00:03:59.250
company back in the '60s and '70s, you read
about, they all had to do sales at one point

00:03:59.250 --> 00:04:00.250
of their career.

00:04:00.250 --> 00:04:01.250
Why?

00:04:01.250 --> 00:04:03.639
Because they had to touch the customer to
know what the customer's like.

00:04:03.639 --> 00:04:04.909
That is my focus.

00:04:04.909 --> 00:04:07.420
I like to hire this [sales] first.

00:04:07.420 --> 00:04:09.470
So if you're not sales, I like to hire this
first.

00:04:09.470 --> 00:04:14.499
When I got started, I'll tell you for myself,
I was this [sales] first, and I'm marketing.

00:04:14.499 --> 00:04:15.499
This [sales and marketing] is me.

00:04:15.499 --> 00:04:16.840
So guess what I needed?

00:04:16.840 --> 00:04:21.530
I needed here [admin], I partnered up with
here [product development], somebody that

00:04:21.530 --> 00:04:23.139
designed the products that I needed.

00:04:23.139 --> 00:04:26.820
So without this, I don't have a product to
sell, so I got product to sell.

00:04:26.820 --> 00:04:28.050
And I needed admin.

00:04:28.050 --> 00:04:29.560
Then I got this [finance and accounting].

00:04:29.560 --> 00:04:32.960
I already had somebody that was helping me
out with this [finance], but then I got this

00:04:32.960 --> 00:04:35.180
and upgraded this to a whole different level.

00:04:35.180 --> 00:04:40.050
So as you're thinking about this with your
business, whatever business you're running.

00:04:40.050 --> 00:04:44.340
Take a sheet of paper out and ask yourself,
what is my strength?

00:04:44.340 --> 00:04:46.509
And what are the opposing strengths that I
need?

00:04:46.509 --> 00:04:48.389
Go recruit that person.

00:04:48.389 --> 00:04:50.090
Go hire that person.

00:04:50.090 --> 00:04:52.500
Stop hiring people that are just like yourself.

00:04:52.500 --> 00:04:55.120
It's cool to be around people that are just
like yourself.

00:04:55.120 --> 00:04:57.310
It's fun when you're around people like yourself.

00:04:57.310 --> 00:05:00.810
That's good maybe when you have a friendship,
but not when you're running a business.

00:05:00.810 --> 00:05:04.229
You're trying to create a business and a business,
if you run out of this [money], you shut down

00:05:04.229 --> 00:05:06.613
the business, you're going back to having
a job.

00:05:06.613 --> 00:05:12.479
So you've got to make sure you make the decision
of who you hire first in a very, very proper

00:05:12.479 --> 00:05:16.419
way or else you won't be in business for too
long.

